title: Respect HRMP channel byte capacity for opaque XCMP notifications

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Fix outbound XCMP capability notifications being exported
      when the HRMP channel has insufficient byte capacity.

      Notifications are now exported and marked as sent only
      when their complete encoded size fits the current
      channel capacity. Otherwise, they remain eligible for
      a subsequent attempt when capacity becomes available.

      No runtime configuration changes or migrations are required.

crates:
  - name: cumulus-pallet-xcmp-queue
    bump: patch
